```
INDUSTRY_PATTERNS_ADOPTED
  tenant-first binding (all five vendors)
  configuration BEFORE credential — group/policy chosen in the console (Cisco, Fleet)
  bounded bootstrap authority, distinct from runtime identity (Fleet's clearest pattern)
  explicit post-onboarding validation as its own stage (Defender)
  LAB/small-first rollout before breadth (Cisco, Sophos)
  live health driven by policy application and check-in, not by installation

NIVXFORGE_DIFFERENTIATORS
  one token → one tenant → one device → one enrolment, burned atomically
    (Elastic tokens can enrol many agents and persist until revoked; we keep ours strict
     and will add a SEPARATE constrained bulk credential rather than relax this)
  the enrolment secret is refused on argv entirely — stdin only
  READY is a composed verdict; SENT ≠ ACCEPTED and an acquisition gap is never benign
  ENROLLED_NEVER_REPORTED already exists as a first-class state: an endpoint that
    authenticated and then sent nothing can never be summarised as healthy
```

